  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Streamlining the response to the HIV epidemic through strengthening national capacities and scaling up prevention and treatment services, with an emphasis on most at risk population groups and civil society participation - Azerbaijan (01-Jan-2016-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Azerbaijan, HIV, Ministry of Health of the Republic of Azerbaijan (MOH Azerbaijan)This program has the following goals: To reduce HIV prevalence among key affected populations and AIDS related mortality in Azerbaijan through improving access of key affected populations to essential HIV prevention, diagnostic, treatment, care and support services.. The objectives of this program are: To create enabling environment and ensure program sustainability.  To ensure universal access to comprehensive HIV treatment, care and support.  To implement evidence-based preventive activities focused on key affected populations</narrative>
  </description>
